---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { href } from "../lib";
---

<Base
  title="Platform build"
  description="Hardened, reusable GitHub Actions workflows, rulesets as code and verified builds, built with your team and handed over for you to own."
>
  <h1>Platform build</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A delivery platform your teams call rather than copy: shared workflows that are secure by default and
    easy to adopt.
  </p>

  <h2>What we build</h2>
  <ul class="ticks">
    <li>Reusable workflows for CI, security scanning, container builds and deployment, versioned and pinned by commit.</li>
    <li>Build provenance on every artefact, verified before anything is deployed.</li>
    <li>Branch and tag protection defined as code and checked for drift, so nobody weakens it quietly.</li>
    <li>OIDC federation to your cloud accounts, with trust scoped to the repository and environment.</li>
    <li>Automated updates for pinned dependencies, arriving as pull requests your team reviews.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>
    Everything is built through pull requests in your repositories, so your team reviews each change as
    it lands. By the end, your engineers have used the platform, changed it and released it themselves.
    You own all of it, with no licence and no dependency on us.
  </p>
  <p>
    The workflows behind this website are an example. <a href={href("demo/")}>See them on GitHub</a>.
  </p>
  <p><a class="button" href={href("contact/")}>Discuss a platform build</a></p>
</Base>
